course: dictionary
lesson: 11342
title: Same letter, different names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change from place to place, even when they point to the same thing. «The letter Z is "zed" in Britain, Ireland, Canada, Australia and most English-speaking places, and "zee" in the USA.» Both words name the same letter, so the context tells you which place the speaker is from.
explain: Zed can also mean sleep, in a funny way. «Catch some zeds» means get some sleep. The clue is the sleep idea, and cartoon sleepers show «zzz», which is why people call sleep zeds. Zeds here is not a letter at all.
explain: When you meet a word with two meanings, swap each meaning into the sentence and see which one makes sense. «I need to catch some letters» does not make sense, so zeds must mean sleep here.
fact: Zed is a noun: one zed, two zeds.
fact: Zed is the name of the last letter of the alphabet, Z, in Britain, Canada, Australia, Ireland and New Zealand.
fact: «Zee» is the name for the same letter in the USA.
fact: «Catch some zeds» means get some sleep.
fact: In maths, z is often a letter that stands for a number, or the third axis.
exercise: What is the letter Z called in Britain? | Zee, used in the USA | *Zed | Zap | Zero
exercise: «Catch some zeds» means what? | Eat a big meal | Run a race | *Get some sleep | Read a letter
exercise: In maths, z often stands for what? | *A number or the third axis | A place on a map | A colour | A day of the week
test: What is the plural of zed? | *zeds | zedz | zed | zedes
test: Which of these countries does NOT say zed? | *USA | New Zealand | Australia | Britain
exam: What does zeds mean in «Catch some zeds before the match»? | Letters of the alphabet | Zebras | *Sleep, because catch some zeds means get some sleep | Numbers on a page
